--- !u!114 &1709852090
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1709852081}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d134c895f42a97b4cb3b4760899213c8, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _documentationText: 'Frame Optimization Example

    Speeds up Dlib face landmark
    detection by downscaling and skipping frames before running detection on live
    input.



    Demonstrates:

    - Reading input frames via MultiSourceToMatHelper
    (webcam, video file, image file, or GPU readback)

    - Using ImageOptimizationHelper
    with MultiSourceToMatHelper for downscale and frame skip

    - Optional OpenCV
    CascadeClassifier face detection instead of Dlib detection

    - Running landmark
    inference on the full-resolution Mat after scaled detection

    - Drawing results
    with DlibOpenCVUtils and previewing via MatToTexture2D



    OpenCV classes
    and APIs used:

    - Mat, Imgproc, CascadeClassifier, MatOfRect

    - MultiSourceToMatHelper,
    ImageOptimizationHelper, OpenCVMatUnityUtils



    Dlib classes and APIs used:

    -
    FaceLandmarkDetector: DetectValueTuple, DetectLandmark

    - DlibOpenCVUtils:
    SetImage, DrawFaceLandmark, DrawFaceRect



    Referring to:

    http://www.learnopencv.com/speeding-up-dlib-facial-landmark-detector/'
  AlignmentSetting: 0
